M4.20 GitHub tree-size query diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28

Error image
-----------
Two read-only GitHub tree requests returned HTTP 404 while the immediately
following commit request succeeded.

Cause
-----
The local zsh loop stored repository and tree SHA in one scalar. Unlike the
assumed shell behavior, zsh did not split that scalar on spaces for `set --`.
The resulting GitHub path was malformed. No repository, branch, server, token,
service, database or provider state was changed.

Risk
----
None to remote or server state. The only risk is recording an incorrect
capacity estimate if the failed output were used.

Rollback
--------
No rollback is required because the request was read-only and returned no
data. This diagnosis file can be reverted with the M4.20 branch if the sprint
is abandoned.

Approved continuation
---------------------
Repeat each read-only request with a literal repository and literal tree SHA,
validate `truncated=false`, and use the returned blob-byte totals only as a
lower-bound source-tree estimate. Do not install, fetch, deploy or alter the
application checkout.
